### Excel Large Data Export API Tests
### Base URL: http://localhost:8080

### =====================================
### 1. Export Products (200k products - default, simple)
### =====================================
# @name ExportDefault
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/excel/products/export?sections=true
Accept: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet

### =====================================
### 2. Export Products (custom count)
### =====================================
# @name ExportCustomCount
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/excel/products/export?count=50000
Accept: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet

### =====================================
### 3. Export with 3 SECTIONS (Styled + DIFF formulas)
### Section 1: Original Data (Blue headers, editable)
### Section 2: Readonly Copy (Green headers, locked style)
### Section 3: DIFF comparison (Orange headers, formulas)
### =====================================
# @name ExportWithSections
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/excel/products/export?count=1000&sections=true
Accept: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet

### =====================================
### 4. Export 50k with 3 Sections
### =====================================
# @name ExportLargeWithSections
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/excel/products/export?count=50000&sections=true&batch_size=5000
Accept: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet

### =====================================
### 5. Export with custom batch size and memory limit
### =====================================
# @name ExportWithConfig
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/excel/products/export?count=100000&batch_size=5000&max_memory_mb=1000
Accept: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet

### =====================================
### 6. Export Progress (SSE Stream)
### =====================================
# @name ExportProgressSSE
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/excel/products/export-progress?count=50000
Accept: text/event-stream

### =====================================
### 7. Get Memory Stats
### =====================================
# @name GetMemoryStats
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/excel/memory-stats
Accept: application/json

### =====================================
### 8. Force Garbage Collection
### =====================================
# @name ForceGC
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/excel/force-gc
Accept: application/json

### =====================================
### USAGE NOTES
### =====================================
#
# SIMPLE EXPORT (1 section):
#   curl -o products.xlsx "http://localhost:8080/api/v1/excel/products/export"
#
# 3-SECTION EXPORT (with styles & DIFF):
#   curl -o products_3sec.xlsx "http://localhost:8080/api/v1/excel/products/export?sections=true&count=1000"
#
# SECTIONS LAYOUT:
#   | Row 1: Title Banner (merged cells, different colors per section)     |
#   | Row 2: Headers (with AutoFilter dropdowns on Section 1 & 2)         |
#   | Row 3+: Data                                                        |
#
#   | Section 1 (A-W)    | Section 2 (X-AT)   | Section 3 (AU-BQ)  |
#   | Original Data      | Readonly Copy      | DIFF Comparison    |
#   | Dark Blue Banner   | Dark Green Banner  | Dark Orange Banner |
#   | Blue Headers       | Green Headers      | Orange Headers     |
#   | Editable           | Locked Style       | Formulas: OK/DIFF  |
#
# FREEZE PANES:
#   - Columns A-E (first 5 columns) are frozen when scrolling horizontally
#   - Rows 1-2 (Title + Headers) are frozen when scrolling vertically
#
# AUTOFILTER:
#   - Filter dropdowns on Section 1 & Section 2 header columns (Row 2)
#   - Section 3 (DIFF) does not have filter
#
# CONDITIONAL FORMATTING:
#   - Section 3 cells show "✓ OK" (green) if Section1 == Section2
#   - Section 3 cells show "✗ DIFF" (red) if values differ
#
# Expected Results (3-section export):
#   - 1k products: ~200KB file, ~1 second
#   - 50k products: ~25MB file, ~15 seconds
#   - Memory should stay under 1.4GB
